","The most common and concerning type of bifurcation lesion is the **""10-point lesion**"" (as described by the **10-point classification** of bifurcation lesions). This classification is used to classify bifurcation lesions based on the degree of stenosis in the proximal and middle segments of the artery. The 10-point lesion is characterized by:  
