3. Bioacterialization: The use of antibiotics can also lead to the development of bacterial bacteria in the human body, which can then contribute to the development of antibiotic-resistant strains of parasites. This is because bacteria can replicate and replicate themselves more quickly than parasites, and they can develop resistance to antibiotics more quickly than parasites.

