   \[
   \text{Normality} = \text{Molarity} \times \text{Number of H}^+ \text{ ions per molecule}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Normality} = 6.00 \, \text{M} \times 2 = 12.0 \, \text{N}
   \]

2. **Calculate the mass of H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) in the 10.0 liters of 2.00 N H\(_2\)SO\(_4\):**
   \[
   \text{Mass} = \text{Volume} \times \text{Normality} \times \text{Molar mass}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Mass} = 10.0 \, \text{L} \times 2.00 \, \text{N} \times 98.0 \, \text{g/mol} = 1960 \, \text{g}
   \]

