1. σ (sigma) molecular orbitals have electron density that is concentrated **directly above and below the internuclear bond** between the nuclei of the atoms.  
2. π (pi) molecular orbitals have electron density that is concentrated **above and below the internuclear bond**, but not directly above or below it.  

Thus, σ orbitals are symmetrical with respect to the intern of the bond, while π orbitals are not.  

\boxed{\text{The π orbital has electron density above and below the internuclear bond, but not directly above or below, while the σ orbital has electron density directly above and below the internuclear bond.}}
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

