Now, let's analyze \( A \cap B \). Since \( b \in B \) and \( b \notin A \), the set \( B \setminus A \) contains \( b \), i.e., \( b \in B \setminus A \).

The symmetric difference \( A \triangle B \) is defined as \( (A \setminus B) \cup (B \setminus A) \). Since \( b \in B \setminus A \), we have \( b \in A \Delta B \).

