\Delta \lambda = \lambda \left( \frac{1 - \cos \theta}{2} \right)
\]

The maximum change occurs when the scattering angle \( \theta = 0^\circ \), which corresponds to head-on scattering. However, the maximum shift is given when \( \theta = 180^\circ \), where \( \cos 180^\circ = -1 \). Substituting \( \theta = 180^\circ \) into the formula:

\[
