The curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y) = \langle f(x, y), g(x, y), 0 \rangle\) is given by:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \begin{vmatrix}
\mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
\frac{\partial}{\partial x} & \frac{\partial}{\partial y} & \frac{\partial}{\partial z} \\
f(x, y) & g(x, y) & 0
\endendmatrix} = \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \cdot 0 - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \cdot f(x, y) \right) \mathbf{i} - \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \cdot 0 - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \cdot f(x, y) \right) \mathbf{j} + \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \cdot g(x, y) - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \cdot g(x, y) \right) \mathbf{k}.
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \boxed{0 \mathbf{i} - \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} \mathbf{j} + \left( \frac{\partial g}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial g}{\partial y} \right) \mathbf{k}} = \boxed{0 \mathbf{i} - \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} \mathbf{j} + \left( \frac{\partial g}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial g}{\partial y} \right) \mathbf{k}}.
\]
